<http://www.spektrix.com/yukonartscentre/event/77201ACHJGSDMKVSDQSJLPVNTKPPQRMCG>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Kaska Voices: An evening of storytelling for future generations";
  schema:description """
	Film, photography, drumming, and conversation are coming together through KASKA VOICES, an opportunity to listen directly to Ross River Dena, deepen connections between communities, and learn about a vision for protection rooted in Kaska knowledge, responsibility, and care for the land: Gūkēyeh Gūs’ān. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Community members from Tū Łī́dlini (Ross River) will be sharing stories, perspectives, and relationships with the lands and waters of Dena Kēyeh (Kaska Country). The evening will include Kaska Drummers, The People of This Land (18 min) paddling film premiere, and a photography slideshow with Peter Mather and Robby Dick with stories from behind their lenses. Kaska Elders and panelists will share perspectives on land stewardship, Indigenous-led conservation, and planning for the future.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Ticket proceeds go to the Tū Łī́dlini Land Guardians.<span><br/></span> <span><br/></span>Event Details<span><br/></span>•	Date: Monday November 9th, 2026<span><br/></span>•	Location: Yukon Arts Centre<span><br/></span>•	Doors open at 5:30 PM | Official event 6:00 PM - 9:00 PM<span><br/></span>•	Tickets are on a sliding scale $15-$30, kids 12 and under free. <span><br/></span>•	Door prizes<span><br/></span>•	Light snacks and refreshments will be provided. Alcohol-free event.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>More details at <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://cpawsyukon.org/kaska-voices\">cpawsyukon.org</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Kaska Voices is a Ross River Dena event organized by CPAWS Yukon and Ross River Dena Council, with support from Yellowstone to Yukon and Wildlife Conservation Society Canada.<span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-11-09T18:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/yukonartscentre/files/d3bb32e4-0ac8-408f-80f3-79cdfa5e988f.jpeg>;
