<http://www.spektrix.com/yukonartscentre/event/71201AVSGMKVRTJBLJQHRLCDKPBMVPLSB>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "The Hobbit";
  schema:description """
	The Yukon Arts Centre is thrilled to present The Hobbit, based on the beloved novel by J.R.R. Tolkien and adapted for the stage by Kim Selody. Join Bilbo Baggins as he leaves the comfort of home for an unforgettable journey across Middle-earth alongside a band of determined dwarves and the wizard Gandalf. Along the way, Bilbo encounters trolls, goblins, elves, giant spiders, riddles, dragons, and discovers that true courage can be found in the most unlikely of heroes. Filled with imaginative storytelling, puppetry, music, and theatrical magic, this family-friendly adventure celebrates friendship, bravery, and the power of stepping into the unknown.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Running Time: Approximately 2 hours, including one 20-minute intermission.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Based on the novel by J.R.R. Tolkien<span><br/></span>Stage Adaptation by Kim Selody<span><br/></span>Licensed by Middle-earth Enterprises<span><br/></span>Creative Team<span><br/></span>Director – Katelyn Morishita*<span><br/></span>Producer – Casey Prescott<span><br/></span>Production Manager – Josh Jansen<span><br/></span>Stage Manager – Kennedy Greene*<span><br/></span>Assistant Stage Manager – Gloria Mok<span><br/></span>Lighting Designer – Martin Nishikawa<span><br/></span>Sound Designer/Music Director – Hannah Mazurek<span><br/></span>Costume Designer – Chantal Lafreniere<span><br/></span>Props Designer – Christopher Gwynne Thompson<span><br/></span>Dragon Puppet Designer – Annie Johnsgaard<span><br/></span>Goblin, Troll, and Spider Puppet Designer - Chantal Lafreniere<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>* Katelyn Morishita and Kennedy Greene appear with the permission of Canadian Actors' Equity Association.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Audience Advisory: The Hobbit is a family-friendly adventure featuring fantasy creatures including trolls, goblins, giant spiders and a dragon, some of which may be frightening for younger children. The production includes staged combat, moments of peril, theatrical lighting effects and the use of haze.<span><br/></span>Recommended for ages 7+.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>
""";
